## Implement Task 3 Lakehouse permission-health UI

Context: Task 3 completes the Settings Lakehouse Health migration to the
permission-only backend response shape and applies the canonical card-integrated
tab rails to Lakehouse, Lakebase, and Neo4j without changing IDs, handlers, or
Bootstrap/ARIA behavior.

Changes:

1. tests/units/front/test_settings_lakehouse_health_permissions.py
   Added strict RED-first frontend contracts for permission-only Health copy,
   `loadDeltaTripleStoreHealth` field usage, icon+text status semantics, and
   canonical tab-rail hierarchy (`card h-100`, `card-body p-0 ob-tabs-wrap`,
   `nav nav-tabs ob-tabs nav-fill`, `tab-content p-3`) with `ob-tab-content`
   removed from the three targeted groups.
2. src/front/templates/settings.html
   Replaced Lakehouse Health description to focus on effective permissions for
   Registry `catalog.schema` and principal; applied canonical tab-card wrappers
   and classes to Lakehouse/Lakebase/Neo4j while preserving existing tab/button/
   pane IDs, modal placement, ARIA attributes, and tab behavior.
3. src/front/static/config/js/settings.js
   Reworked `loadDeltaTripleStoreHealth` to consume only permission-focused
   fields (`registry_catalog`, `registry_schema`, `principal`, `accessible`,
   `operational`, `permissions`, `error`), render one row per permission with
   inherited source, escape all server-provided values, and expose overall
   status via icon + text (not color-only).
4. tests/units/front/test_lakehouse_materialization_ui.py
   Updated the legacy Settings-health expectation now that Health no longer
   depends on materialization/view-count behavior.

