## Fix Task 3 browser blocker and low findings

Context: Task 3 follow-up addresses the browser blocker on horizontally
scrollable Settings tab rails and the remaining low findings on Lakehouse
Health response handling and accessibility semantics.

Changes:

1. tests/units/front/test_settings_lakehouse_health_permissions.py
   Added RED-first contracts for standards-based nearest-inline tab rail
   scrolling on Bootstrap activation/focus in `deltaTabs`, `lakebaseTabs`,
   `neo4jTabs`, plus Health `resp.ok` guard and live status container semantics.
2. src/front/static/config/js/settings.js
   Added Settings-only tab rail auto-scroll wiring using `scrollIntoView` with
   `{ inline: 'nearest', block: 'nearest' }` on `shown.bs.tab` and `focusin`
   events for the three page-level rails, without changing shared tab CSS/IDs.
3. src/front/static/config/js/settings.js
   Hardened `loadDeltaTripleStoreHealth` to check `resp.ok` before parsing JSON
   and throw into the existing error UI path for HTTP failures.
4. src/front/templates/settings.html
   Added `role="status"` and `aria-live="polite"` to `deltaHealthResult` to
   announce Health refresh results accessibly without layout/geometry changes.

